BufferedReaderandBufferedWritermake reading and writingtext filesfaster.

These classes are usually combined withFileReaderandFileWriter, 
which handle opening or creating the file. The buffered classes then make reading/writingfasterby using a memory buffer.

UseBufferedReaderwithFileReaderto read each line of a file:

Java gives you several ways to read files. Here's when to pick each one:

### Code Snippets

```
Example
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.FileReader;
import java.io.IOException;

public class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader("filename.txt"))) {
      String line;
      while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
        System.out.println(line);
      }
    } catch (IOException e) {
      System.out.println("Error reading file.");
    }
  }
}
The output will be:
Some text from filename.txt
